    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1125">

                <pb facs="1023" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg709"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ecuadorian Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Córdova</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-13">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">January 13, 1915</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 16]</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 25th ultimo, in further relation to the
                    representations that have been made by France and Great Britain to Ecuador in
                    regard to the alleged violation of neutrality by Ecuador in permitting German
                    men-of-war to use the Galápagos Islands as a base of supplies and
                    observation.</p>
                <pb facs="1024" n="710" xml:id="pg710"/>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform you that the Department has communicated to
                    the French and British Embassies the substance of your note, and the substance
                    of that part of your note of December 3, 1914,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1125-f1"/>
                    which treats of the violation of Ecuadorian neutrality in the Galápagos
                    Islands.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
